<onlyinclude>'''Self-organized criticality''' (SOC) describes a proposed class of dynamical systems that evolve toward critical-like, scale-free behavior without precise external tuning of a control parameter.

== Explanation ==
A simplified sandpile model receives grains slowly. When a pile at one site exceeds a threshold, it redistributes grains and may trigger a cascade. Cascades can range from small to large. Real sandpiles do not necessarily follow the same statistics.

